{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHeldKeyCodes(): Ref<Record<string, string>>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHeldKeyCodes.ts#L31","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHeldKeyCodes.ts:31"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue composable that returns a reactive ref mapping currently held key names to their physical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful for debugging which physical key was pressed (e.g. distinguishing\nleft vs right Shift via \"ShiftLeft\" / \"ShiftRight\")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Ref"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive ref containing record mapping normalized key names to their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <kbd v-for=\"key in heldKeys\" :key=\"key\">\n      {{ key }} <small>{{ heldCodes[key] }}</small>\n    </kbd>\n  </div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHeldKeyCodes(): Ref<Record<string, string>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHeldKeyCodes.ts:31](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHeldKeyCodes.ts#L31)\n\nVue composable that returns a reactive ref mapping currently held key names to their physical `event.code` values.\n\nThis is useful for debugging which physical key was pressed (e.g. distinguishing\nleft vs right Shift via \"ShiftLeft\" / \"ShiftRight\").\n\n## Returns\n\n`Ref`\\<`Record`\\<`string`, `string`\\>\\>\n\nReactive ref containing record mapping normalized key names to their `event.code` values\n\n## Example\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <kbd v-for=\"key in heldKeys\" :key=\"key\">\n      {{ key }} <small>{{ heldCodes[key] }}</small>\n    </kbd>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHeldKeyCodes\ntitle: useHeldKeyCodes\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHeldKeyCodes(): Ref<Record<string, string>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHeldKeyCodes.ts:31](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHeldKeyCodes.ts#L31)\n\nVue composable that returns a reactive ref mapping currently held key names to their physical `event.code` values.\n\nThis is useful for debugging which physical key was pressed (e.g. distinguishing\nleft vs right Shift via \"ShiftLeft\" / \"ShiftRight\").\n\n## Returns\n\n`Ref`\\<`Record`\\<`string`, `string`\\>\\>\n\nReactive ref containing record mapping normalized key names to their `event.code` values\n\n## Example\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\nconst heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <kbd v-for=\"key in heldKeys\" :key=\"key\">\n      {{ key }} <small>{{ heldCodes[key] }}</small>\n    </kbd>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n"}
